I have a 3D voxel game with cubed chunks sized 16x16x16, spanning infinitely in all 6 directions, generated by 3D perlin noise.

--- Generation stages ---

~ Initialization ~
Uninitialized - Set chunk positions.
Islands - Set initial island stone

~ Cross-Chunk ~
Surface - Set biome dependent surface blocks (based on if air is above)
Decorations - Lay terrain decorations such as trees, grass blades, flowers
Lighting - Set light blocks according to probe-based algorithm
Meshing - Mesh all chunks optimized with neighbor checks

--- Lighting algorithm ---
Skylights come from all 6 directions, but don't exist inside either caves
or player made structures.

~ Skylight placement ~
All blocks start with light level of 0, unless emissive.
Start from each block at the edge of render distance, cast inwards from
all 6 directions. If solid block is hit, terminate. Otherwise, continue
until at render distance center, setting every air block to 15 along
the way.

~ Light propagation ~
Using BFS algorithm.
